  "content": {
    "id": "p40-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Find any stationary points on the curve $f(x)=x^4+8x^3+16x^2-1$ and their nature.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(0,-1)$ minimum, $(-2,15)$ maximum, $(-4,-1)$ minimum.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=4x^3+24x^2+32x\\\\&=4x(x^2+6x+8)\\\\&=4x(x+2)(x+4).\\end{align*}$$\nAt stationary points, $f'(x)=0$, so $x=0,-2,-4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}f(0)&=-1,\\\\f(-2)&=(-2)^4+8(-2)^3+16(-2)^2-1\\\\&=15,\\\\f(-4)&=(-4)^4+8(-4)^3+16(-4)^2-1\\\\&=-1.\\end{align*}$$\n$$f''(x)=12x^2+48x+32.$$\nAt $x=0$, $f''(0)=32>0$, so $(0,-1)$ is a minimum.\n\nAt $x=-2$, $f''(-2)=48-96+32=-16<0$, so $(-2,15)$ is a maximum.\n\nAt $x=-4$, $f''(-4)=192-192+32=32>0$, so $(-4,-1)$ is a minimum.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
